course: dictionary
lesson: 10234
title: Toffee in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Toffee is a hard or chewy brown sweet made by boiling sugar and butter. When you read a sentence, the words around toffee give you clues. «After that the balls come back straight away, sometimes with a toffee.» A sweet given as a reward fits well here, so toffee is the sweet itself.
explain: Writers also use toffee to make comparisons. «Hot glass is soft like toffee.» Toffee is soft when it is heated, so the comparison tells you that hot glass is soft and bendy, not sticky and brown. Ask yourself: what does the word show me about the thing it is compared to?
explain: Some phrases use toffee in a special way. Someone who «can't do it for toffee» is very bad at it. You can't tell this from the single word, so read the whole phrase. When a phrase surprises you, check the words around it before you decide what it means.
fact: Toffee is a hard or chewy brown sweet made by boiling sugar and butter.
fact: «Toffee» can also mean a single sweet of this kind, as in «a toffee».
fact: Toffee apples are eaten at autumn fairs and on Bonfire Night in the UK and Ireland.
fact: In science and cooking, toffee shows how sugar changes when it is heated.
fact: «Can't do it for toffee» means very bad at doing something.
exercise: «After that the balls come back straight away, sometimes with a toffee.» What is a toffee in this sentence? | *A sweet | A shoe | A toy | A ball
exercise: «Hot glass is soft like toffee.» What does this comparison tell you? | Hot glass is cold and hard | Hot glass is brown and sticky | Hot glass is heavy like a stone | *Hot glass is soft and bendy, like heated sugar
exercise: Sam can't draw for toffee. What does this phrase mean? | Sam draws with toffee | Sam loves drawing | *Sam is very bad at drawing | Sam draws very quickly
test: Toffee is made by boiling which two ingredients? | Milk and flour | *Sugar and butter | Eggs and cream | Salt and water
test: Toffee shows what happens to sugar when it is heated. Is this a science idea or a cooking idea? | Only music | Only maths | *Both science and cooking | Only sport
exam: In the sentence «The drink tastes of cherry-tart, custard, pine-apple, roast turkey, toffee and hot buttered toast», what kind of word is toffee? | An adjective | An adverb | *A noun | A verb
